nline Parallel Run.',\n    type: 'Game',\n    genre: 'Simulation',\n    source: 'Densha de Go!',\n    series: 'Densha de Go!',\n    players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Lever R2/L2 or W/S, neutral R1/N, emergency brake L1/Backspace, point and call Cross/E, horn Square/Space, ATS confirm Triangle/Q, view Circle/C. Mouse: wheel and cab buttons.',\n    tags: ['3d', 'first-person', 'retro', 'vehicles', 'arcade', 'story']\n  }\n};\n})();\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":1,"newStart":1,"newLines":56,"lines":["-(() => { const DH = window.DH; DH.ABOUT = { info: {}, testing: [], engine: [], prompt: [] }; })();","+/* About & Credits data. tools/exit.mjs writes exit-interview.json from this same object, so the screen and the file never disagree. */","+(() => {","+'use strict';","+const DH = window.DH;","+DH.ABOUT = {","+  info: {","+    date: '2026-11-04 05:02:38',","+    source: 'Densha de Go! (the train-driving simulation series): a notched master controller, stopping on a marker, a timetable kept to the second, ATS, point-and-call calls.',","+    plan: 'PLAN.md',","+    genre: 'Simulation (train driving with arcade scoring)',","+    perspective: 'First-person cab in pseudo-3D, with chase and front cameras and a side-view Stop Cam replay after every stop',","+    tech: 'my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine: game loop, input, menus, Shell pause/settings/controls, Dialog, Humanoid, chip audio, headless advance), plain JavaScript, a custom pseudo-3D rail renderer (src/30-render.js), AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0. Tests: Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 (Chromium).',","+    artDirection: \"The engine's native look: 427x240 low-resolution pixels, hue-shifted shading and the pixel font, with a hand-built segment-based pseudo-3D world (stations, strips, buildings, trains, catenary, fog, night lights).\",","+    animation: \"The engine's Humanoid rig for the talking portraits, plus code-driven animation: the lever handle and needle, the pointing glove, wipers, rain, crowd sway, crossing gates, the Stop Cam replay.\",","+    audio: 'All code: the engine chip synth for effects and songs, plus a Web Audio train soundscape (rumble, rails, wind, motor, brake squeal, horn, rain), station departure melodies and Animalese-style gibberish voices for every character.',","+    online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: the Parallel Run for 1 to 4 players, with the other players shown as coloured ghost trains. Passes the hub harness.',","+    testing: 'Headless Node tests (119 checks: physics, ATS, signals, stops, the whole career played by the autopilot through the real scenes, attract mode, dev mode), a Playwright browser smoke test, and the AI Hub harness (1, 2 and 4 players, latency and loss, host leaves).',","+    research: 'Read the engine card (README, API.md, the road kit) and the AI Hub README, and followed PLAN.md. No web research; the source is described from general knowledge.',","+    environment: 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser tests in headless Chromium, player browser unknown',","+    model: 'Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium',","+    usage: 'unknown'","+  },","+  testing: [","+    'How many issues did testing catch? About 9 real game issues.',","+    'How many were critical? 3: the train could freeze at a hair above 0 km/h and never be judged, a stop more than 80 m past the marker was never judged, and a finished shift left a flag set that hung the next one.',","+    'Most helpful test: the scripted career, where the autopilot drives all six stages through the real title, map, briefing, drive and results scenes.',","+    'Least helpful: screenshots from software-rendered headless Chromium for anything that depends on timing; they only show a frame.'","+  ],","+  engine: [","+    'What did you like most? Exact fixed steps with game.advance, so the whole game plays headless and deterministically, plus the free pause, settings and controls screens.',","+    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Input.tap() marks the device as touch, which tripped my touch-only gate in tests; and the pause-menu items need game.resume() themselves.',","+    'Most important thing to build yourself: the rail renderer (segments, platforms, strips, trains, catenary, fog, night) and the train physics, ATS and timetable.',","+    'Hardest part: the engine had no multi-track or rear-camera road module, so everything projected had to be written from scratch on top of the pixel primitives.',","+    'What did you change? Dialog voice can be a function (for gibberish speech); the glyph default is PlayStation; ChipAudio.bus() and noiseBuffer() for the game\\'s own sound; and Options is ignored while Create is held in a hub session. See ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',","+    'One thing to change: a first-class pseudo-3D road/rail module with multiple tracks, long side objects and rear cameras.'","+  ],","+  prompt: [","+    'What did you like most? A concrete plan with a clear core loop, and hard rules (no stubs, tests behind one command, the hub harness as a gate).',","+    'What was confusing? PLAN.md is very large and prescribes more than the TASK needs (a local duel, engine forks, rig poses), so triage was needed; and the title RNG step was already done by the plan.',","+    'Hardest thing: breadth. Menus, dev mode, attract mode, story, voices, hub and a new renderer all have to be finished in one session.',","+    'What would you change? Split the plan into must, should and could, and say which engine patches are optional.'","+  ],","+  aiHub: {","+    name: 'Densha de Halo!',","+    tagline: 'Hello by train. Stop on the mark.',","+    description: 'Drive the Halo Line ring railway: notch the lever, obey signals and ATS, point and call, and stop on the marker on the second. A short story, six shifts and an online Parallel Run.',","+    type: 'Game',","+    genre: 'Simulation',","+    source: 'Densha de Go!',","+    series: 'Densha de Go!',","+    players: '1–4',","+    controls: 'Lever R2/L2 or W/S, neutral R1/N, emergency brake L1/Backspace, point and call Cross/E, horn Square/Space, ATS confirm Triangle/Q, view Circle/C. Mouse: wheel and cab buttons.',","+    tags: ['3d', 'first-person', 'retro', 'vehicles', 'arcade', 'story']","+  }","+};","+})();"]}],"originalFile":"(() => { const DH = window.DH; DH.ABOUT = { info: {}, testing: [], engine: [], prompt: [] }; })();\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TQGwdaNcLtkjitdGhEopnp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
