DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    5405 Nov  4 05:40 exit-interview.json\n--- head order\n<!doctype html> <html lang=\"en\"> <head> <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> <script> /*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */ (function (root) {   'use strict';   if (root.AIHub) return;    var VERSION = '1.4.0';   var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;   var HELLO_T\n\n--- hub meta\nname=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"\nname=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"\nname=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\"\nname=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Drive the Halo Line Parallel Run: stop each train on the mark, on time, smoothly. The best score wins.\"\nname=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lever: R2/L2 or W/S. Neutral R1/N. Emergency brake L1/Backspace. Point and call: Cross/E. Horn: Square/Space. ATS confirm: Triangle/Q. View: Circle/C.\"\nname=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\"\n--- features in bundle\nController or keyboard required      2\nDev Mode                             3\nRESET TO DEFAULTS                    1\nDEMONSTRATION                        1\nplaystation                          6\nAIHub.connect                        1\nvoiceChar                            3\nRetry from last station              1\nXbox                                 2\n--- TODO/stub scan\n589: *  from, a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp.mjs replaces when the site deploys (e.g. 'a1b2c3d 2026-10-07');\nall 119 checks passed\nall 120 checks passed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ELzhMbcYdSvhAJAPtN8BYg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuXR5ycyT8nAV88nXPA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle and exit-interview are in place and I've gone through every TASK.md requirement. All are implemented except one, the local split-screen Duel, which TASK.md never asks for. The only place the words TODO or placeholder appear in the bundle is a comment inside the engine source, not game code.\n\nI can't hear sound in this environment. For audio I only know the audio code ran with no errors while the game was played, not how it sounds.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single bundled `.html` in the folder root, named per STAGE.md | `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html` (1.4 MB). It loaded from `file://` and went from the title to the Halo map. |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt feedback in the reply and in an in-game About screen | In the reply above. The About screen has five pages (Source Information ×2, then the three feedback sections), shown in a screenshot. |\n| `exit-interview.json` parses and every field is filled | Parsed with a script; the generator fails on any empty field except `series`. |\n| Build on the engine, engine changes allowed | v0.85.2; four changes logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`. |\n| New art assets and animations for the source | The rail renderer and cab, plus the lever, needle, pointing glove, Stop Cam, wipers and crossing gates; seen in screenshots of all three views, night and storm. |\n| Audio all in code, gibberish voices | No audio files. Every character has a gibberish voice, a hooked-up Dialog and subtitles. Audio ran with no errors in a browser run with horn, call and ATS keys pressed. |\n| Online via the AI Hub library | The page has the hub meta tags and `session.js` first in `<head>`. The harness passed with 1, 2 and 4 players, with 150 ms latency and 5% loss, and with the host leaving. |\n| Feature-complete, long enough to show everything | Six career stages, Free Run and the Parallel Run. The test suite plays all six stages through the real title, map, briefing, drive and results scenes to the ending. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | Opened from the pause menu in a browser and the screenshot shows the sliders. A test checks the d-pad moves a slider and that reset restores the defaults. |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle, any input exits | Test: attract starts after 10 s idle on the title, keeps running, and any input returns to the title. |\n| 10-foot, controller-first UI | Every screen works with pad or keyboard; prompts follow the last device used. PlayStation glyphs are the default, with an Xbox option in Settings. |\n| Keyboard feels native; mouse aims and clicks | Test: W/up moves the lever, N goes to neutral, Backspace is the emergency brake. In a real browser, clicking a notch, the wheel, the N, EB and CAM buttons all worked. Menus move focus on hover. |\n| Touch-only shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus Settings, attract keeps running | The string is in the build and the title has a Settings entry. I did not test it on a real touch device. |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | Scan of the bundle found none in game code. |\n| Narrative tone like the source | Terse calls such as \"SIGNAL, GREEN!\", formal station announcements and a short story across the six shifts. |\n\n**Checks:** `node test/run.mjs` gives 119 passed, and with `BROWSER=1` 120 passed. The browser smoke test also covers the results, game over, ending, log, help, about and free-run screens drawing with no console errors.\n\n**Duel:** the local split-screen Duel comes from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. TASK.md's multiplayer requirement is the AI Hub integration, which is done and passes the harness. It is also listed under \"Not done\" in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_