{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdW2V88xBYq7d3mZ53RxT1","type":"tool_result","content":"wrote DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html 1.38 MB\nwrote exit-interview.json 5402 bytes\nall 124 checks passed\nafter 11 s idle: attract no errors\nharness 2: pass: true no page errors \nharness 4|&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1: pass: true no page errors\n[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: src/65-about.js, src/60-ui.js. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0738416c-8908-4884-b93b-1b7b7f6ce2f9","uuid":"14aa1ec2-91a8-4171-a677-81ea6e50c08e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:47:45.524Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"wrote DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html 1.38 MB\nwrote exit-interview.json 5402 bytes\nall 124 checks passed\nafter 11 s idle: attract no errors\nharness 2: pass: true no page errors \nharness 4|&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1: pass: true no page errors","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: src/65-about.js, src/60-ui.js. Call Read before editing.]"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RdW2V88xBYq7d3mZ53RxT1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuvxXjFpgbdCrZ2cDip","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the local split-screen Duel, so everything TASK.md asks for and everything PLAN.md lists is now in the build, with two qualifiers. I can't hear audio in this environment, and the touch-only behaviour was tested with touch emulation only.\n\nThe bundle is `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html` in the folder root, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. The JSON was regenerated and parses.\n\n**Duel:** \"LOCAL DUEL\" is a new title-menu entry. Two players share one keyboard on the same Parallel Run stage, each with their own train and half of the screen (a screenshot confirmed the split view renders).\n- **Player 1:** W/S lever, F call, G horn, H ATS, R emergency brake, T neutral.\n- **Player 2:** Up/Down lever, `.` call, `/` horn, `,` ATS, L emergency brake, `;` neutral.\n- It ends with a winner screen and a rematch option.\n\n**Checks on the final bundle:**\n- **Test suite:** `node test/run.mjs` passes all 124 checks (5 new for the Duel).\n- **Touch-only:** the touch-emulation test still shows the message and runs the attract demo, with no errors.\n- **Hub harness:** the 2-player and the 4-player latency/loss runs both pass.\n\n**Audio:** an analyser on the master output showed audible, varying signal (RMS 0.006–0.039) while the autopilot drove, but I have not heard it by ear.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:38\n- **Source:** Densha de Go! (the train-driving simulation series)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Simulation (train driving with arcade scoring). First-person cab in pseudo-3D, with chase and front cameras and a side-view Stop Cam after each stop.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine), plain JavaScript, a custom pseudo-3D rail renderer, AI Hub client `session.js` 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native low-resolution pixel look (427×240), with a hand-built segment-based world: stations, buildings, trains, catenary, fog, night lights.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig for the talking portraits, plus code-driven animation: lever and needle, pointing glove, wipers, rain, crowd sway, crossing gates, Stop Cam replay.\n- **Audio:** All code. The engine chip synth for effects and songs, a Web Audio train soundscape (rumble, rails, wind, motor, brake squeal, horn, rain), a departure melody per station, and gibberish voices for each character.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: the Parallel Run, 1–4 players, others shown as coloured ghost trains. Plus the local two-player Duel.\n- **Testing:** Headless Node tests (124 checks, including the autopilot playing all six stages through the real scenes and the Duel), a Playwright browser smoke test, touch emulation, an audio-level check, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** Read the engine card and the AI Hub README, followed PLAN.md. No web research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser tests in headless Chromium, player browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 9 real game issues.\n- **How many were critical?** 3. The train could freeze just above 0 km/h and never be judged. A stop more than 80 m past the marker was never judged. A finished shift left a flag set that hung the next one.\n- **Most helpful test:** The scripted career, where the autopilot drives all six stages through the real title, map, briefing, drive and results scenes.\n- **Least helpful test:** Screenshots from software-rendered headless Chromium for anything timing-dependent; they only show a frame.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Exact fixed steps with `game.advance`, so the whole game plays headless and deterministically, plus the free pause, settings and controls screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `Input.tap()` marks the device as touch, which tripped my touch-only gate in tests. The pause-menu items also need `game.resume()` themselves.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The rail renderer (segments, platforms, strips, trains, catenary, fog, night) and the train physics, ATS and timetable.\n- **Hardest part:** The engine has no multi-track or rear-camera road module, so everything projected had to be written from scratch on the pixel primitives.\n- **What I changed in the engine:**\n  - `Dialog` voice can be a function, for the gibberish speech.\n  - The glyph default is PlayStation.\n  - Added `ChipAudio.bus()` and `noiseBuffer()` so the game's own sound follows the volume settings.\n  - `Options` is ignored while `Create` is held in a hub session.\n- **One thing to change:** A first-class pseudo-3D road/rail module with multiple tracks, long side objects and rear cameras.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A concrete plan with a clear core loop, and hard rules: no stubs, tests behind one command, the hub harness as a gate.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is very large and asks for more than TASK.md needs (a local duel, engine forks, rig poses), so I had to triage. The title RNG step was already done by the plan.\n- **Hardest thing:** Breadth. Menus, dev mode, attract mode, story, voices, hub and a new renderer all had to be finished in one session.\n- **What I would change:** Split the plan into must, should and could, and say which engine patches are optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":408522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999},"output_tokens":818,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_man