{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghv5KyYESwCdn1m6kLcJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Control radio voice is now as loud as the others: peak 0.038, against 0.029–0.059 for the rest. The bundle `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050238.html` is rebuilt in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` was regenerated and parses, and `node test/run.mjs` passes all 124 checks.\n\nI have not heard the audio and have not run touch-only on a real touch device; neither is possible in this environment. Voices were checked by measurement only. Touch-only was checked with touch emulation: the title shows \"Controller or keyboard required\", only Settings stays selectable, and the attract demo starts after 10 s idle. All other TASK.md features are implemented and checked, including the local Duel and the AI Hub Parallel Run.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:38\n- **Source:** Densha de Go! (the train-driving simulation series)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Simulation (train driving with arcade scoring). First-person cab in pseudo-3D, with chase and front cameras and a side-view Stop Cam after each stop.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine), plain JavaScript, a custom pseudo-3D rail renderer, AI Hub client `session.js` 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native low-resolution pixel look (427×240), with a hand-built segment-based world: stations, buildings, trains, catenary, fog, night lights.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig for the talking portraits, plus code-driven animation: lever and needle, pointing glove, wipers, rain, crowd sway, crossing gates, Stop Cam replay.\n- **Audio:** All code. The engine chip synth for effects and songs, a Web Audio train soundscape (rumble, rails, wind, motor, brake squeal, horn, rain), a departure melody per station, and gibberish voices for each character.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: the Parallel Run, 1–4 players, others shown as coloured ghost trains. Plus the local two-player Duel.\n- **Testing:** Headless Node tests (124 checks, including the autopilot playing all six stages through the real scenes and the Duel), a Playwright browser smoke test, touch emulation, audio-level and voice measurements, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** Read the engine card and the AI Hub README, followed PLAN.md. No web research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser tests in headless Chromium, player browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 9 real game issues.\n- **How many were critical?** 3. The train could freeze just above 0 km/h and never be judged. A stop more than 80 m past the marker was never judged. A finished shift left a flag set that hung the next one.\n- **Most helpful test:** The scripted career, where the autopilot drives all six stages through the real title, map, briefing, drive and results scenes.\n- **Least helpful test:** Screenshots from software-rendered headless Chromium for anything timing-dependent; they only show a frame.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Exact fixed steps with `game.advance`, so the whole game plays headless and deterministically, plus the free pause, settings and controls screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `Input.tap()` marks the device as touch, which tripped my touch-only gate in tests. The pause-menu items also need `game.resume()` themselves.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The rail renderer (segments, platforms, strips, trains, catenary, fog, night) and the train physics, ATS and timetable.\n- **Hardest part:** The engine has no multi-track or rear-camera road module, so everything projected had to be written from scratch on the pixel primitives.\n- **What I changed in the engine:**\n  - `Dialog` voice can be a function, for the gibberish speech.\n  - The glyph default is PlayStation.\n  - Added `ChipAudio.bus()` and `noiseBuffer()` so the game's own sound follows the volume settings.\n  - `Options` is ignored while `Create` is held in a hub session.\n- **One thing to change:** A first-class pseudo-3D road/rail module with multiple tracks, long side objects and rear cameras.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A concrete plan with a clear core loop, and hard rules: no stubs, tests behind one command, the hub harness as a gate.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is very large and asks for more than TASK.md needs (a local duel, engine forks, rig poses), so I had to triage. The title RNG step was already done by the plan.\n- **Hardest thing:** Breadth. Menus, dev mode, attract mode, story, voices, hub and a new renderer all had to be finished in one session.\n- **What I would change:** Split the plan into must, should and could, and say which engine patches are optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":417263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":787,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0738416c-8908-4884-b93b-1b7b7f6ce2f9","uuid":"f5931ea3-9545-47bb-b8bb-49e0c1e65a51","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:49:48.351Z","request_id":"req_011Cghv5KaEXGoC83MnD9rNK"}
